SOURCE REVIEW (2.9 — no product edit)
========================================================================

`ooda/oodac/c_emit_ident.oo` L129–131 (HEAD-clean, 228 lines):

```
if id == "println" {
    p = c_emit_println(toks, p, n, e);
    return c_pack_pos_env(p, e);
}
```

`ooda/oodac/c_emit_print.oo` `c_emit_println` (HEAD-clean, 87 lines):

```
per-arg token IDENT
  if __sec__sn == "1" → c_secret_refuse_println_ident
then c_emit_expr_c + oo_print_*
```

No alias resolve on arg names. emit-c still refuses alias because
`c_emit.oo` L86 runs `check_secret_println_sinks` **before** stmt emit.

`ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret.oo` `check_secret_println_sinks` L175–193
(264 lines; WT dirt = 7.10 `str_slice` + 2.10 `__sec_sink__` only):

```
sid = c_secret_resolve_alias(env, id)
if sid == "println" || sid == "eprintln":
    optional skip LPAREN
    walk tokens to RPAREN
    IDENT → c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved(env, sid, nm)
```

`ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret_guard.oo` `c_secret_emit_guard` (228 lines):
- `sink = c_secret_resolve_alias(env, t)`
- sealed list includes println/eprintln → `c_guard_scan_idents`
- **callers:** `c_emit_lower.oo` L90 (free-call), `c_emit_call.oo` L82
  (method). **Not** `c_emit_println`.

`ooda/oodac/c_emit_let.oo` L168–169 records `__alias__f` on
`let f = println` (CRIT 2.4). Live on emit env **if** lower is reached.
Stmt `println` never reaches lower.

`ooda/oodac/check_drive.oo` WT: secret **before** typecheck (6.1).
Host 07:49 ELF is still type-then-secret. println is a known name →
check dual-path SECRET refuse still fires on this host.

